    "name": "Édifice Jean-Talon",
    "notes": "Édifice Jean-Talon (Complexe H et J, 1969–1972), brutalist. From aerial photos over Wilfrid-Laurier and over Grande Allée: beige concrete fins (~0.9 m every 1.5 m, dark slots between) on every wall, no windows; a scalloped arcade on the Wilfrid-Laurier ground floor, broken by four solid stair towers; gravel roofs with parapets the fins rise past. Façade frame on Wilfrid-Laurier, Place George-V (−along) to Avenue George-VI (+along). Massing: a 17 m wing on Grande Allée, a 22 m range on Wilfrid-Laurier, the 24 m George-V block with a plant room and a square deck, a glazed slot with red rails, the green-roofed centre block, and the George-VI block set back, stepping up 26 → 29 → 32 m.",
